# class List extends Array { constructor() { super(); this.tag = 1 } }; list = new List; flat = list.flat(); return flat.tag
# flat asks the class of its receiver for a species and fills what that has made: it defines elements and stores the length. It deletes nothing there, redefines no name and freezes nothing,
# so the field that the constructor of the class fills keeps its facts, and a read of it gives what the constructor has stored.
